course: dictionary
lesson: 300
title: Reading science words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from science and health, and you can often work them out from the words around them. «Iron is needed to make red blood cells, and too little causes anaemia, which makes people tired and pale.» The sentence tells you what anaemia causes: tiredness and paleness. It also tells you the cause: too little iron.
explain: Anaemia is a noun, so it names an illness. Read it as a whole word and ask: what would fit here? Then test your meaning in the sentence. Does «too little iron causes an illness where the blood is not healthy enough» still make sense? Yes, so you have understood it.
explain: Science texts often use a second clue: a test. «A blood test can check iron levels.» A doctor can use a blood test to see whether someone has enough iron, which helps find out whether they have anaemia. The dictionary confirms the meaning, so you can check your guess.
fact: Anaemia is an illness where the blood does not have enough healthy red blood cells or iron.
fact: A person with anaemia often feels very tired, weak and pale.
fact: Iron is needed to make red blood cells.
fact: Foods with iron include spinach, beans, red meat and fortified cereals, which help prevent anaemia.
fact: In American English the spelling is anemia, but the meaning is the same.
exercise: «Too little iron causes anaemia, which makes people tired and pale.» What does anaemia make people feel? | Very hungry | Full of energy | Hot and sweaty | *Tired and pale
exercise: Which food from the health lesson helps prevent anaemia? | Sweets | Crisps | Fizzy drinks | *Spinach
exercise: The American spelling of anaemia is... | anaemia | *anemia | anaemya | aneamia
test: «A blood test can check iron levels.» What can a blood test check, according to the sentence? | The weather | Your shoe size | *Iron levels | The length of your hair
test: If someone feels very tired and pale, which illness might a doctor check for? | Hay fever | Toothache | Sunburn | *Anaemia
exam: Which food from the health lesson helps prevent anaemia? | Sweets | Fizzy drinks | *Beans | Crisps
